From 3d9ca49a97bc7aff3132b9aa9e77ce134b254efb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 02:45:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] fix(ui): a gauge length edit never draws the library body
 over wider steel

The generic component editor found the built-in holder by name and drew
its outline at the new gauge length. A user holder with a library name
and a wider body under the flange envelope then got a body smaller than
its steel. ComponentGeometry::regauged_holder now accepts the library
outline only when the holder's outline is the library's at its own gauge
length and the new outline is that outline with one cylindrical section
made longer or shorter. Each other case is refused by name.

Fixes #4496

